            "review_title": "Review at Danang Tower Steakhouse & Soju Bar",
            "review_text": "Gerry C\nBusselton, Australia93 contributions\n0\nDon't Go There\nMar 2023 • Couples\nHaving checked in to the excellent Vinpearl Hotel to celebrate my wife's birthday, we decided to have dinner at this place located on the 37th level and were not aware that this establishment was a completely independent business and NOT managed by the hotel, it quickly became apparent that the staff had received little training if at all, the steak which we ordered to be well done and cooked on a stone BBQ next to our table was handed to us still almost raw and ordered the meat to be cooked more which they didn't seem to understand, the side salad was very unappetizing and the quality of the meat was questionable at a cost of over 2 million dong ( no drinks ) we found this price absolutely exorbitant the ultimate being that after returning to our room my wife spent almost the entire night in the bathroom being violently sick , the only positive of this disastrous evening was the breathtaking view of the lights of Danang city. I would strongly suggest to the Vinpearl Hotel management that the lease for this disgraceful restaurant be terminated because if hotel guests are not aware as was the case with us that they are not commercially connected it may reflect badly on the overall excellence of the otherwise great hotel. In conclusion, I cannot recommend this so-called restaurant at all particularly as there are so many very good restaurants in Danang City from which to choose.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 17, 2023",
